**Theorem 7.3 (balanced post-update literal-query lower bound).** Under
Definition 7.2's exact hypotheses,

$$
|L|\,4^R\ge|\mathcal F_s|\ge K_s.
\tag{DAF.19}
$$

In particular, if $|L|\le2^b$ then

$$
b+2R\ge\log_2K_s.
\tag{DAF.20}
$$

Proof. Initially every source has the same initial boundary and the same
accepted-update response and current tag-0 boundary. Fix one supplementary label
and an acquired literal-answer branch. Equal complete acquired data gives the
same next numerical request, actual context, local operation, archive access,
or literal address. TM30.1/TM30.2 preserve equality of numerical boundaries and
original responses under every original numerical action, including actual
acceptance and rejection. Literal Reads preserve the source and its numerical
boundary. PR57.T3 gives equality of the full original paid microtrace between
literal responses; the added-port visibility hypothesis does the same for each
literal segment. All archives, copies, verification and outputs are computations
on those acquired data. No complete executed event is discarded by this argument.

Contract the intervening determined segments only for counting. Each remaining
literal node has at most four reply branches. Sourcewise finite termination and
common deterministic stopping make the terminal reply paths prefix-free, including
variable stopping depths. Induction gives at most $4^R$ leaves per label; this
is the credited existing four-valued decision-tree argument.

Suppose two distinct initial sources reached one terminal leaf. Their complete
acquired states and all actual choices on that branch agree. Lemma 7.1 says
their current actual trees are still distinct, even after the common accepted
prelude, further accepted actions and rejects. At some literal address those
current trees differ. The common local decoder, receiving the same terminal
state and that address with no source access, would give the same answer for
both, contradicting the required exact current-tree response. Hence each leaf
contains at most one initial source. Summing over labels proves (DAF.19);
(DAF.18) and $|L|\le2^b$ give (DAF.20).

This proof cannot grant the full leaf word for free: unlike the bracket regime,
the selected balanced fiber can contain different words. Its source-dependent
ingress is restricted to the numerical response stream, added literal replies
and complete label. Publishing private word data, rejected candidate values or
source-dependent literal latency would change these hypotheses.

